Below is a self-contained Unity C# MonoBehaviour you can attach to a 2D projectile (Rigidbody2D + Collider2D). While you click/drag on the object, it shows a series of UI dots in a Canvas that visualize the predicted trajectory. When you release, it launches the object in that direction and hides the trajectory dots and the optional direction UI image.

Notes:
- Works with a Screen Space Overlay Canvas (recommended), but also supports Screen Space Camera/World Space if you assign the Canvas and its camera.
- Uses simple kinematics for prediction (no collisions/ricochets in the preview). You can later extend to step the physics scene for more accurate predictions if needed.
- For simplicity, the script uses OnMouseDown/OnMouseDrag/OnMouseUp. Make sure your projectile has a Collider2D to receive these events. This also works with a single touch on mobile.

Setup:
1) Create a UI Canvas (Screen Space - Overlay recommended).
2) Create a small UI Image to use as a dot (prefab). Assign it to Dot Prefab in the inspector.
3) (Optional) Create a UI Image (e.g., an arrow) to visualize direction. Assign to Direction Image in the inspector.
4) Add this script to your projectile GameObject. Assign:
   - Target Canvas (the Canvas that will hold the dots)
   - Dot Prefab (UI Image)
   - (Optional) Direction Image
5) Ensure the projectile has Rigidbody2D and a Collider2D.

